WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit
4: Advertising and Persuasion.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.499
Every day, you are surrounded by messages
designed to grab your attention, change your mind,

3
00:00:10.579 --> 00:00:12.751
or convince you to buy something.

4
00:00:12.831 --> 00:00:20.327
From billboards towering over busy Mogadishu streets to
sponsored posts sliding through your social media feed,

5
00:00:20.407 --> 00:00:22.101
advertising is everywhere.

6
00:00:22.181 --> 00:00:23.535
But how does it work?

7
00:00:23.615 --> 00:00:27.220
What techniques do advertisers use to persuade people?

8
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:34.796
And how can you, as a critical thinker, tell the difference
between honest information and clever manipulation?

9
00:00:34.876 --> 00:00:40.529
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:40.609 --> 00:00:49.025
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand passages about advertising techniques, persuasion,

11
00:00:49.105 --> 00:00:53.383
and ethical marketing, and discuss their ideas confidently.

12
00:00:53.463 --> 00:01:01.067
You will also identify and use prepositions preceding
nouns correctly in phrases like on sale, in stock,

13
00:01:01.147 --> 00:01:04.982
for a limited time, at a discount, and with interest.

14
00:01:05.062 --> 00:01:10.523
You will also form and use passive
voice sentences in the present and past:

15
00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:17.541
"The product was launched by the company" and
"The advert is designed to attract young people."

16
00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:20.274
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:01:20.354 --> 00:01:27.052
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: aptitude,
adversary, cunning, momentum, bonanza, concession.

18
00:01:27.132 --> 00:01:32.231
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:36.259
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:36.339 --> 00:01:43.282
The reading sequence includes The Power of Persuasion and
Adverts Everywhere: An Interview about Advertising Ethics.

21
00:01:43.362 --> 00:01:44.130
Read actively.

22
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.308
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

23
00:01:48.388 --> 00:01:52.243
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

24
00:01:52.323 --> 00:01:56.253
The first language focus is Prepositions Preceding Nouns.

25
00:01:56.333 --> 00:02:03.288
Prepositions are small words that show the relationship
between a noun and the rest of the sentence.

26
00:02:03.368 --> 00:02:09.901
In advertising language they sit directly before
nouns to build fixed phrases such as on sale,

27
00:02:09.981 --> 00:02:18.272
in stock and at a discount, and learning each phrase as one
complete unit makes your English sound natural and precise.

28
00:02:18.352 --> 00:02:25.940
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:30.293
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: My Advertising Story.

30
00:02:30.373 --> 00:02:34.851
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:34.931 --> 00:02:38.319
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:38.399 --> 00:02:41.924
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:42.004 --> 00:02:43.622
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:43.702 --> 00:02:50.928
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:51.008 --> 00:02:54.470
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:54.550 --> 00:03:02.661
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
